<BaseLayout
  title="Music | Ray Weiss"
  description="Music. Ray Weiss recorded as Le Rug, with Sweet Bulbs and Butter The Children before that. Brooklyn projects from a former life."
>
  <main class="doc">
    <div class="doc__frame">
      <header class="page-heading">
        <h1>Music</h1>
        <p class="dek">
          Ray recorded as Le Rug. Before that, Sweet Bulbs and Butter The Children. The instruments
          are sold; the catalog is still up.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose-body">
        <p>
          Le Rug was Ray's main music project from Brooklyn for years. Full discography at <a
            href="https://lerug.bandcamp.com/music">lerug.bandcamp.com</a
          >, also on Spotify, Apple Music, and iTunes. The Bandcamp bio phrases it as "basically Ray
          Weiss & Friends." These days the focus is on the games and software, but the catalog is
          still up for anyone who wants to dig.
        </p>
        <p>
          CatalogDNA once analyzed this four-hundred-track catalog as its development dataset. The
          canonical structural match came back as Pete Burns / Dead or Alive. One of the Le Rug
          albums is titled <a href="https://lerug.bandcamp.com/album/party-with-peter-burns"
            ><em>Party With Peter Burns</em></a
          >, so the album's homage is also its fingerprint. For the full recursion, see the <a
            href="/catalogdna">CatalogDNA page</a
          >.
        </p>

        <h2>Selected releases</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <a href="https://lerug.bandcamp.com/album/party-with-peter-burns"
              ><em>Party With Peter Burns</em></a
            >
          </li>
          <li><em>BOZO DEFENESTRATOR</em></li>
          <li><em>Flabby Wings Ray Weiss</em></li>
